  "kanji": "音",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 音\ntitle: sound\njlpt: 4\ntags: [jlpt-n4, grade-1, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 9\nradical: 音\nradicalNumber: 180\nonyomi: [オン, イン, -ノン]\nkunyomi: [おと, ね]\ndistractors: [意, 立, 春]\n---\n\n# 音 — sound\n\n**Strokes:** 9 · **Key (radical):** 音 (no. 180) · **JLPT:** N4 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n音 is **sound**: a noise, a musical tone, or a speech sound, depending on the word.\nThe ordinary standalone word is 音（おと）.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic:** see [立](立.md) above a [日](日.md)-shaped box and imagine a speaker standing\non a sound box. This is a visual association, not the character's verified origin.\n\n## Readings\n\nThis table is selective; the source reading -ノン is preserved in metadata but is not a general substitute for オン.\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| オン | on | 音楽 おんがく (music); 発音 はつおん (pronunciation) |\n| イン | on | 母音 ぼいん (vowel) |\n| おと | kun | [音](../words/音.md) おと (sound; noise) |\n| ね | kun | 音色 ねいろ (tone quality; timbre) |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [音](../words/音.md) おと — sound; noise\n- 音楽 おんがく — music\n- 発音 はつおん — pronunciation\n- 音色 ねいろ — tone quality; timbre\n\n## Notes\n\n声（こえ）usually draws attention to a voice or an animal's call; 音 is the broader everyday word for sound.\n雨の音（あめのおと）means \"the sound of rain.\"\n\n[意](意.md) adds [心](心.md) below 音. [立](立.md) alone lacks the lower box.\nLearn おと and ね in their words rather than exchanging them freely.\n",
